scription":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-25T15:49:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T15:17:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproduced in 4.0.4.stable, 4.3.stable and 4.4.stable.\n- Not reproduced in 3.6.stable\n- Seems to be introduced with 4.0\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Linux Mint 22.1 (Xia) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (nvidia; 550.120) - AMD Ryzen 5 3500X 6-Core Processor (6 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI am working with small objects and tried setting the grid minimum size to 0.01m instead of the default 1m.\nWhen zooming out and in, the grid seems to disappear.\n\nWorking correctly in Godot 3.6:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68fa433c-a9cb-4d08-b9a5-521a2c2d3a07\n\nBug in Godot 4.4:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53703882-b3d2-4e8d-b76a-afa676f44280\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet in `Editor Settings -> Editors -> 3D -> Grid Division Level Min` to `-1` or `-2`. Zoom out and in in the editor and watch the grid change. (Videos in Issue Description for reference)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis can be done by creating an empty project and changing the editor setting and using the zoom.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/1046